3. Run \`go test -race ./internal/cli/...\` — the race detector should not flag the \`assignedEpicID\` access in \`buildCommand\`.

## Summary

Add a two-tab interface (Details / Logs) to the IssueDetailPanel, replacing the current single-scroll-view layout. The Details tab contains all existing content (description, design, notes, dependencies, comments). The Logs tab shows agent logs specific to this issue by using the issue's assignee field to connect to the agent's terminal logs — reusing the existing useAgentTerminalLogs hook and LogViewer component already used by AgentDetailPanel.

This replaces the existing task-only log tabs (Details/Planning/Implementation) with a cleaner two-tab model that works for all issue types.

## Technical Approach

- Follow the tab pattern already established in AgentDetailPanel (ARIA roles, CSS styling, state management)
- Reuse \`useAgentTerminalLogs\` hook for the Logs tab, passing \`issue.assignee\` as the \`agentName\`
- The existing task-specific log tabs (Planning/Implementation using \`useTaskLogPolling\`) will be replaced by this unified tab approach. The Planning content (design markdown) already appears in the Details tab. Implementation logs are subsumed by the agent Logs tab.
- Tab bar goes between the blocking banner and the scrollable content area
- Only show Logs tab when the issue has an assignee (otherwise there's no agent to show logs for)
- Default to Details tab; reset to Details when issue changes

