## Summary

Show agent assignment and activity information on both In Progress and Review (Needs Review) cards in the web UI Kanban board. Currently, the AgentRow (avatar, status dot, name, activity text) only renders on in_progress cards. This task extends it to also render on review cards, so operators can see which agent submitted a task for review.

## Technical Approach

This is a targeted one-line condition change in IssueCard.tsx plus corresponding test updates. The existing AgentRow component and all supporting infrastructure (getAgentByName, parseLoomStatus, getStatusLabel, avatar/dot color utilities) are already in place and work correctly for in_progress cards. We simply need to widen the gate.

**Key design decision — activity text on review cards:**
For in_progress cards, the AgentRow shows the agent's *live* status (e.g., "Working", "Planning"). For review cards, the assigned agent has likely moved on to another task, so showing their live status would be misleading. Instead, we show a static "Submitted for review" activity string for review cards, regardless of the agent's current live status. This makes the intent clear: the assignee on a review card is the *submitter*, not someone actively working.

**Approach:**
- Rename `showAgentRow` to a condition that includes both `in_progress` and `review` columns
- Add a `isReviewColumn` boolean to select the appropriate activity text
- For review cards: pass `activity="Submitted for review"` with no status dot (agent is no longer actively working this task)
- For in_progress cards: behavior is unchanged (live agent status)

