## Problem

renderPrompt (internal/cli/prompts.go:38-54) contains three panics. Two are safe (embedded resources validated at compile/test time), but the third (line 50-51, tmpl.Execute) is reachable at runtime when a user-provided override template in loom-prompts/*.md references struct fields that don't exist on promptTemplateData.

## Previous Design Issues

The previous design inlined the embedded template loading logic directly in the Execute fallback path, duplicating what loadTemplate already does. It also didn't track whether an override was used, meaning if the embedded template itself failed Execute, it would pointlessly retry with the same content.

## Approach: Track Override Origin, Fallback Only When Warranted

Modify loadTemplate to return whether the content came from an override. On Execute failure, only attempt embedded fallback if an override was active. If the embedded template fails Execute, that's a real bug — keep the panic.

## Implementation

### File: internal/cli/prompts.go

**Change 1: loadTemplate signature (lines 63-83)**

Change return type from (string, error) to (string, bool, error) where the bool indicates whether an override was loaded:

