## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **No repo filter active (selectedRepos = []):** isGrouped is false, flat list renders (exact current behavior). No visual change.
2. **Filter active but no agents match any selected repo:** All agents appear in "Other" section. Each selected repo group shows with count 0. This correctly communicates "these repos have no assigned agents."
3. **Agent has no repo field (undefined):** Falls into "Other" group. This handles agents from single-repo workspaces that don't set the repo field.
4. **Agent.repo matches a selected repo exactly:** Goes into that repo's group. Matching is case-sensitive (repo names come from the server, same source for both filter and agent data).
5. **Very long repo names in group header:** CSS truncation with text-overflow: ellipsis prevents layout breakage in the 282px sidebar width.
6. **All agents match selected repos (no "Other" agents):** The "Other" section is conditionally rendered (only when other.length > 0), so it simply doesn't appear.
7. **localStorage errors (private browsing, quota):** All localStorage operations are wrapped in try/catch. Defaults to empty collapsed state (all groups expanded).
8. **Rapid filter changes:** groupAgentsByRepo is a pure function called on each render — no stale state concerns. useRepoFilter updates synchronously from URL.

